{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791575928,"nonce":"aGrx19gl8wmYl/X9iLxlZB8qU5U=","message":"Decision: fetch_log rows are per hop under that hop's own request_hash; conditional headers and ttl apply per GET hop, so a redirecting URL always costs the cheap 3xx hop but its target can still 304 or hit ttl. A ttl hit makes no request and writes no fetch_log row. Reason: fetch_log has no final_url/location column, and logging cache hits would bloat the log without recording any exchange.","files":null}]}